  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nShowers will continue through Sunday, tapering off throughout \nthe day as the system departs. Snow levels Sunday will have \nlowered to 5.5-7kft MSL (increasing from west to east). These \nsnow levels are higher than previous model runs consistent with \na faster system trend. Snowfall will likely be limited to the \nmountains Sunday through Monday morning. In areas below the snow\nlevel less than 0.1 inches of rain is forecast, with only a \ntrace to 0.03 inches forecast in the lower valleys. Sunday \nafternoon and evening will feature gusty winds following the \ncold frontal passage, with west to northwest gusts of 20-40 mph \nin the Snake River Plain.\n\nBeginning Monday, the area will be dry with a warming trend\nthrough Thursday, although seasonable temperatures are \nanticipated throughout. Fog and stratus is possible Monday\nand Tuesday mornings with the recent precipitation and at the \nbeginning of the warming trend. While there will be multiple \nopportunities for weak shortwaves to pass over the area, \nmoisture will be limited and the shortwaves will just result in \nperiods of increased high clouds.",
